  "query_preview": "..\nNext 7 Days (Through Friday)...\n\nAreas of precipitation (60-90% chance) will gradually move south \nthis morning and exit the region by this afternoon. Weak \ninstability over the region may allow for a few rumbles of \nthunder. Isolated showers (10-30% chance) may linger over the \nmountains and nearby plains through this afternoon. Precipitation\ntotals look to range from a few hundredths to a trace over the \nnorth, to between 0.50 to 0.75 inches of precipitation, with \nlocally higher totals over the northerly upslope regions of the \nsouthern mountains and foothills. There is a moderate to high \nchance of at least 0.25 inches of precipitation south and west of \na Melville to Billings to Alzada line. \n\nOver the mountains, snow levels will fall to around 7,500 feet \nthis morning, and the higher peaks above 9,000 feet can expect \nseveral inches of snow. Snow will likely impact the Beartooth \nHighway and a Winter Weather Advisory remains in effect this \nmorning. Be prepared for impacts to recreation and travel in the \nhigh country!\n\nTonight into Sunday morning, frost will be a concern for locations\nover the foothills and higher hills as temperatures drop into the\nmid 30s. Currently, the highest chance is 30-50% over the \nSheridan foothills. Sensitive vegetation may be affected!\n\nConditions trend drier through Monday, outside of occasional \npieces of energy bringing isolated shower and weak thunderstorm \nactivity to the region in the afternoons/evenings. By late \nTuesday into Wednesday, a more active wave is possible under upper\nlevel northwest flow. Occasional pieces of energy will continue to\nmove through the flow through the end of the work week, allowing\nisolated afternoon/evening showers and thunderstorms to continue.\nArcher",
